@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
    ViewData["Description"] = "What Utah Course Compass is and where its numbers come from: the University of Utah's public class schedule and grade summary.";
    ViewData["Canonical"] = "/About";
    ViewData["Listed"] = true;
}

<div class="page-head center">
    <h1>About</h1>
</div>

<div class="about">
    <p>Hi, I'm Sam. I'm a CS student at the University of Utah. I built this website because the U's registration system looks like it was made in 1998. Here, course information, grade distributions, and Rate My Professors links are all in one place, in something I hope is easier to use.</p>

    <h2>Where I got the data</h2>
    <p>Course information and grade distributions are scraped from the U's <a href="https://class-schedule.app.utah.edu/" rel="noreferrer">class schedule</a> and <a href="https://data.utah.edu/dashboards-and-data/course-grade-summary/" rel="noreferrer">grade summary</a>. The grade summary doesn't say who taught a section, so a professor's distribution comes from matching their sections in the schedule to the same sections in the summary.</p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>The U suppresses any letter-grade count under five, so in a small class the bar graph might not match the statistics shown. Professor averages are pooled from their sections and weighted by headcount, which might be off due to suppression and can nudge a professor's average slightly. I checked pooled averages against published course grade totals and found the median difference to be under 0.01, with 95% within 0.05, so the effect is negligible.</p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>Utah Course Compass is not affiliated with or endorsed by the University of Utah.</p>
</div>
